ction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411818 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186411770 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411818 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "008191e4-1343-56f9-9409-2e7c06d48454" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411868 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411818 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411868 #edb/ref 1069 "q-34177" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411868 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411868 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)=⟨t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ for $t>0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411868 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a3fef8c5-dedd-5425-a060-104bbe0a3652" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411868 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $T(t)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the parameter t. Since we are given the curve r(t) parametrized by the parameter \nt (not the arc length s), we will use the following formula for the curvature\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ &  \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nsince $t>0.$ \n\nHence, the corresponding unit tangent vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, the curvature for  $t>0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{1}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433616 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186433631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433616 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186433632 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433616 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186433633 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433616 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433616 #edb/ref 1045 "Introduction to Curvature" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433616 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186433631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433616 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433616 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049196 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433616 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "2b8eb350-78af-5600-9e7a-328caccbfa84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433617 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433617 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433617 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1251bed4-415d-5590-a871-e4a9657e13d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433618 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433618 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433618 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1367431b-f708-53d0-907c-401baf44b1b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433619 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433619 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433619 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "481e6b9f-c5af-58b8-b98e-c12965a43b0e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433620 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}